src/3rdparty/walkontable/dist/
# The dev pages here and the output directories below exist at the package root only, so their rules
# start with a slash. Git applies a rule with no slash, or only a trailing one, at every depth, where
# these would also match sources such as `src/i18n/languages/xx-XX.ts` or a new `src/i18n/es/`
# directory and keep them out of `git status`. The outputs below the root have rules of their own
# above, and `node_modules/` matches at every depth on purpose, because installs nest. Nothing has
# written `es/` or `commonjs/` since the ES and CJS builds moved to `tmp/`, but `clean` still removes
# them. Pinned by the repository's scripts/__tests__/gitignore-scope.test.mjs.
/dev*.html
/dev*.js
/dev*.ts
npm-debug.log

/dist/
/languages/
node_modules/
/commonjs/
/es/
/coverage/
/tmp/
/tmp_styles/
/styles/
src/styles/handsontableStyles.js
src/styles/handsontableStyles.ts
# The json report of a mutation run: `evals/score.mjs --mutate` runs Stryker from this directory, and
# the root's `reports/mutation/` matches the repository root only.
/reports/mutation/

# Figma "Design Tokens" plugin export consumed by scripts/themes/figma (user-provided)
scripts/themes/figma/tokens.json
